# Scope declaration for tools/gates/no-broker-dep.sh (the R-SOV-1 gate, lifted from kotva).
#
# no-broker-dep:self-broker: this repo IS the Pier broker/coordinator reference implementation that BROKER_RE names, not a product depending on it.
#
# Why a repo-level declaration instead of individual :allow-file markers, and why that is
# an honest use of the escape hatch rather than a way to dodge it:
#
# BROKER_RE defaults to `pier|vulos-relayd`. Both terms are THIS repo's own names —
# Cargo.toml's header calls it "Pier — the broker (coordinator) reference implementation
# of the KOTVA standard", and cmd/vulos-relayd/main.go is pier's own Go reverse-tunnel
# relay binary (a legacy binary name for the same product, not a second broker). R-SOV-1
# asks "does this PRODUCT depend on the broker?" — applied to the broker's own source tree
# the question is malformed, not merely satisfied: every crate path under this checkout
# (.../pier/crates/admin, .../pier/crates/pier-gateway, ...) matches BROKER_RE purely because
# the checkout directory is named "pier", and essentially every source file, README and
# comment legitimately says "Pier" in the sense of naming itself. Running the gate here
# produced ~300 structural false positives, none of them a dependency edge.
#
# Marking every one of those files individually with :allow-file would either bury that
# marker's accountability under bulk, mechanical use, or train reviewers to rubber-stamp a
# wall of exemptions — which is the exact failure the marker mechanism exists to prevent.
# A single, committed, greppable, reasoned repo-level file is the narrower instrument here.
#
# This declaration is honoured ONLY because it states a reason on the marker line itself —
# see tools/gates/no-broker-dep.sh's CONFIGURATION section and selftest controls
# ('self_broker_reasoned' / 'self_broker_unreasoned') in kotva, which prove a reason-free
# version of this file is deliberately NOT honoured and the gate runs its normal scan
# instead. Pier is not thereby exempt from anything else: a genuine dependency by THIS
# repo on some OTHER broker would still need its own honest accounting; there is none.
